# Line endings and binary handling.
#
# This repo is authored on Windows and deployed to Linux (Helios). Without
# this file, `core.autocrlf=true` writes CRLF into every checked-out text
# file, and a shell script that reaches a Linux host with CRLF fails as
# `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env sh^M` — a documented failure in this
# organisation's fleet notes, not a hypothetical.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises everything to LF in the repository AND in
# the working tree, so what is committed is what runs on the server, and
# every editor in use handles LF fine. It also ends the several-hundred-line
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning on every commit, which was training
# everyone to ignore git's output.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files where LF is not a preference but a correctness requirement: these
# are executed by a POSIX shell or a Linux container.
*.sh              text eol=lf
*.mjs             text eol=lf
*.sql             text eol=lf
Dockerfile*       text eol=lf
*.yml             text eol=lf
*.yaml            text eol=lf
.githooks/*       text eol=lf
.env.example      text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts genuinely want CRLF.
*.ps1             text eol=crlf
*.bat             text eol=crlf
*.cmd             text eol=crlf

# HLS media fixtures. MPEG transport streams use the `.ts` extension, which
# collides with TypeScript — Prettier has parsed these as source and `tsc`
# has reported "File appears to be binary", each fixed locally by whoever
# hit it first (see docs/13c). Declaring them binary here fixes it at the
# origin for every tool that consults gitattributes, and stops git
# attempting line-ending conversion on video, which would corrupt it.
#
# Deliberately scoped to the fixture directory: `*.ts` globally would mark
# the entire TypeScript codebase binary and destroy every diff.
packages/media/fixtures/**/*.ts   binary
packages/media/fixtures/**/*.m3u8 text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never convert, never diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4  binary
*.pdf  binary

# Generated. Collapse in reviews so a real change is not buried in noise,
# but still diffable on request with `git diff --text`.
pnpm-lock.yaml                        linguist-generated=true -diff
packages/contracts/openapi/go/**      linguist-generated=true
packages/contracts/openapi/*.json     linguist-generated=true
services/ledger/internal/store/sqlcgen/** linguist-generated=true
services/voucher/internal/store/sqlcgen/** linguist-generated=true
